B8 are exhausted). Opponents have various exposed melds: next player has a pung of B8; across has chow W3,W4,W5 and pung F1; previous player has chows T4,T5,T6 and pung B1 and chow W1,W2,W3.  \\nMy history shows I have made two Chi actions (Chi W7, Chi T2) and discarded many mid-range tiles and honors. Currently, I cannot call Pung, Kong, or Chi because it's my turn to discard from my hand. Valid actions are to discard one tile from my hand: J3, W9, F2, or T7.  \\n\\n**Evaluation:**  \\nI need to aim for a winning hand of 14 tiles (4 melds + pair), worth at least 8 fan. Currently I have three chow melds exposed, so I still need one more meld and a pair.  \\nMy hand has potential patterns:  \\n- **Half Flush** (6 fan) possible if I keep only W suits and honors (my exposed melds include W6-8 and T suits; T suits don't count toward half flush if I aim for W+honors only). Actually Half Flush requires all tiles to be either honors or tiles of one suit only. My exposed melds include two T-suit chows, which would break Half Flush unless I can change them (but melds are fixed). So Half Flush is impossible because of T-suit melds.  \\n- **All Chows** (2 fan) \\u2014 I already have three chows, could go for fourth chow (but one more meld needed, could be a pung too).  \\n- **Prevalent Wind/Seat Wind** (2 fan each) \\u2014 I have F2 tile (South Wind) in hand; if I keep it and later make a pung of F2, I could score both Prevalent and Seat wind fan.  \\n- **Dragon Pung** (2 fan) \\u2014 J3 in hand; making a pung of White Dragon possible.  \\n- **All Simples** (2 fan) \\u2014 my exposed chows are all simples (no terminals/honors), and my remaining hand tiles W9 is terminal (9), F2 is honor, J3 is honor \\u2014 so if I keep any terminal/honor, I lose All Simples.  \\n- **No Honors** (1 fan) \\u2014 requires no honor tiles in hand at win; currently have F2 and J3, so not eligible if I keep them.  \\n- **Mixed Straight** (8 fan) \\u2014 I have three chows from different suits? W6-8 (W), T1-3 (T), T7-9 (T) \\u2014 T suits repeat, so not three different suits, so Mixed Straight not possible.  \\n\\nPotential scoring paths:  \\n1. **Go for a quick win with simple hand + some fan from winds/dragons** \\u2014 need one meld (pung or chow) and a pair.  \\n2. **Discard honors/terminals to aim for All Simples + All Chows** \\u2014 that\\u2019s only 4 fan, not enough 8 fan minimum. So must combine with other patterns (e.g., Concealed Hand, Self-Drawn, etc.) or get pung of dragon/wind for extra fan.  \\n3. **Try for Half Flush** \\u2014 impossible due to fixed T-suit melds.  \\n4. **Try for Mixed Triple Chow or Pure Triple Chow** \\u2014 not possible with current hand.  \\n\\nLooking at tile availability:  \\n- F2: 3 left unseen (total 4, none shown in melds/discards? history shows previous played F3, F1 pung by across, I played F4 earlier; no F2 shown discarded). So F2 has 3 available for pung.  \\n- J3: 3 left unseen (total 4, none shown discarded? across played J3 once; I have one J3). So J3 also 3 left for pung.  \\n- W9: 3 left unseen (total 4, previous played W9 once, I have two W9). Possible pair/pung.  \\n- T7: 2 left unseen (total 4, I have one, next played T7 once, previous played T7 once).  \\n\\nIf I discard W9, I lose chance for W9 pung. If I discard F2, lose chance for F2 pung (Prevalent+Seat wind). If I discard J3, lose chance for J3 pung (Dragon Pung). If I discard T7, T7 is simple, might help All Simples but reduces chance for T7 chow/pung.  \\n\\nGiven the 8-fan requirement, likely need at least one pung of honor/dragon/wind to reach 8 fan when combined with other small patterns.  \\nPossible minimal winning fan:  \\n- Dragon Pung (2) + Prevalent Wind (2) + Seat Wind (2) + All Chows (2) = 8 fan exactly.  \\nFor that, I\\u2019d need pung of J3 and pung of F2 \\u2014 but I only have one each in hand now, and need two more of each \\u2014 possible but tough.  \\nAlternatively, one pung of F2 (2+2=4 fan) plus All Chows (2) plus maybe Concealed Hand (4 if fully concealed) or Self-Drawn (1) etc.  \\n\\nGiven my exposed melds, Concealed Hand impossible (melds exposed). So must rely on Pung of terminals/honors for fan.  \\n\\n**Best discard now** is the tile that is safest (not giving opponent win) and keeps flexibility for collecting honors for pung.  \\n\\nCheck discards:  \\n- J3: safe? J3 unseen 3, but across played J3 earlier, maybe they need it? Still relatively safe.  \\n- W9: terminal, relatively safe except someone might need for Thirteen Orphans? Unlikely.  \\n- F2: South wind, my seat wind + prevailing wind, maybe someone else also needs? But no F2 shown discarded. Possibly safe.  \\n- T7: mid tile, could complete someone\\u2019s chow (T5-T6-T7 or T6-T7-T8 or T7-T8-T9). More dangerous.  \\n\\nAlso consider my own hand: I have two W9, one F2, one J3, one T7. If I discard T7, I have two W9 (potential pair/pung), F2 and J3 (potential pung). That keeps two possible honor pungs and a pair.  \\nIf I discard W9, I lose a potential pair and keep T7 (less useful).  \\nIf I discard F2 or J3, I lose one honor pung chance.  \\n\\nGiven I need pung for fan, keeping both F2 and J3 is good. So discard T7 to aim for All Simples? But then I lose All Simples because I still have W9 terminal. So better to discard W9 to keep All Simples possible? But then I lose a pair candidate (W9). Actually if I discard W9, my hand is T7, F2, J3 \\u2014 no pair, and T7 is simple, F2/J3 honors \\u2014 so still no All Simples (has honors). So All Simples impossible if I keep honors.  \\n\\nSo maybe forget All Simples, focus on collecting honors. Keep F2, J3, and a pair candidate (W9). Discard T7 as least useful for pung.  \\n\\n**Reason:**  \\nT7 is a simple suited tile that doesn\\u2019t contribute to needed fan patterns as much as honors/terminals. Discarding it retains both F2 and J3 for potential pungs (which give multiple fan each) and keeps W9 as possible pair/pung. It also avoids giving opponents an easy chow (though T7 is somewhat live). It\\u2019s the most flexible choice to pursue a hand with Dragon Pung + Prevalent/Seat Wind pungs to reach 8 fan.  \\n\\n**Answer:** Play T7\"}"}
